From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 06:57:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 013/184] segacd: publish the live screen base to the servant
 each VBL
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The servant read the framebuffer from a fixed address chosen at E2,
which holds only while EmuTOS leaves the screen where it booted it.
The file viewer takes the whole screen, and once the framebuffer moves
the servant converts whatever now occupies the old address — text read
as four bitplanes, which tiles the entire display with repeating
letter-shaped cells and clears again when the viewer exits. The VBL
handler now publishes v_bas_ad so the servant can follow it.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 4c9c672..4b3f5cc 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -132,6 +132,12 @@ void segacd_int_2_c(void)
         }
     }
 
+    /* Tell the servant where the screen really is. It used to assume the
+     * boot-time address, which breaks the moment anything moves the
+     * framebuffer (the file viewer does) — the servant then converts
+     * whatever now lives there, filling the display with garbage. */
+    *(volatile UWORD *)0xFF8020 = (UWORD)(((ULONG)v_bas_ad) >> 8);
+
     int_vbl();
 }
 
